{
 "question": "Do the four kinds of model that read past weather + river gauge miss the same onsets, and how many of the onsets that all of them miss does the LSTM warn of when it is given more information?",
 "quick_mode": false,
 "headline": "1 day ahead, all four kinds of model given past weather + river gauge (ridge regression, random forest, LSTM, Transformer) miss the same 461 of the 611 onsets (75.5%); of those, the LSTM given rain up to the evening of the issue day warns of 16.9%, and the LSTM given the perfect weather forecast, an upper bound that cannot be had in practice, of 61.8%. (A warning is a forecast above the high-flow level itself; the Transformer is the two-seed model of the cost comparison.)",
