 "how_to_read": {
  "shares": "every share is a fraction between 0 and 1; all counts are for the test years with the basins pooled; models and also_missed_of_lstm_misses are keyed by prediction set, and kinds gives the plain name of each (prediction_sets: its family as in flood.MODEL_COL, the script that wrote it, its seeds)",
  "n_onsets": "high-flow days whose forecast was issued while the river was still at or below the high-flow level",
  "onsets_dropped": "onsets of the flow record left out because a prediction set has no forecast for the day (0 = every set is scored on every onset)",
  "basin_days_scored": "all days whose forecast was issued while the river was at or below the level: the onsets and the days that stayed at or below it",
  "models": "per prediction set: onsets warned (hits) and missed (misses); false_alarms = warnings, issued while the river was at or below the level, for days that stayed at or below it; pod = hits / n_onsets; far = false_alarms / (hits + false_alarms)",
  "missed_by_all_kinds": "onsets that none of the kinds of model warned of; share = of n_onsets; share_if_independent = the product of the kinds' own shares of missed onsets; share_if_independent_by_basin = the same product taken basin by basin, weighted by the basin's onsets (the basins differ in how many of their onsets the kinds miss)",
  "warned_by_any_kind": "onsets with a warning from at least one kind (share = of n_onsets); false_alarms = days that stayed at or below the level with a warning from at least one kind; far = false_alarms / (count + false_alarms)",
  "warned_by_all_kinds": "onsets that every kind warned of; share = of n_onsets",
  "of_missed_by_all": "of the onsets missed by all kinds: those the LSTM given more information warned of; share = of missed_by_all_kinds.count",
  "lstm_misses": "count = onsets the LSTM (lstm_wq) misses; warned_by_another_kind = those of them that at least one other kind warned of, share = of count",
  "also_missed_of_lstm_misses": "of the onsets the LSTM (lstm_wq) misses: those the other kind also misses; share = of lstm_misses.count; share_if_independent = the other kind's own share of missed onsets (misses / n_onsets), which is what share would be if the two models' misses were unrelated; share_if_independent_by_basin = the same with the other kind's share of missed onsets taken basin by basin",
  "seed_to_seed": "the same between two single seeds of the LSTM: of the onsets one seed misses, the share the other also misses; min and max over every ordered pair of seeds; pairs lists them (misses = onsets the first seed misses, count = those the other seed also misses); share_if_independent as above",
  "at_levels_chosen_on_validation": "the same counts as under l1, l2 and l3 (same keys) when every prediction set warns at the level chosen for it on the validation years, not at the high-flow level itself; levels = that level per prediction set and lead, as a multiple of the high-flow level; rule = how it is chosen; null if no level could be chosen",
  "checks": "stored_counts: one row per prediction set, lead and results file; key holds <count> for hits, misses and false_alarms; asserted = the script stops if the row is not equal. levels_chosen_on_validation: one row per prediction set and lead for which 06_flood_analysis.py stored a level"
 },
